  "id": "COMPOUND:21966 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Farnesiferol A is shown to have a target relationship with COLO-824, which is subsequently identified as a target of multiple entities, including Npc154515 and 1,3-Dibromo-2-propanone. These entities are all linked to DNA polymerase iota, suggesting a potential pathway through which Farnesiferol A may influence the activity of this enzyme. The evidence indicates that Farnesiferol A may act as a modulator of COLO-824, which in turn affects DNA polymerase iota through various downstream targets. The final score of 0.5562 suggests a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, supported by multiple indirect pathways. The mechanism likely involves the regulation of COLO-824, which could either directly or indirectly influence DNA polymerase iota through its downstream targets. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, but the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain, requiring further experimental validation.",
